id: pm-ul9rye
title: "Nightly coverage, quality, and Windows tests exceed serial job budgets"
description: "Manual Nightly Validation run 35905763390 at 544c19398 passed Windows Node 24 and three other platform legs, but Ubuntu Node 24 spent the 20-minute job budget running full coverage and static quality serially. The static gate reached the final mutation step before job cancellation, so the nightly result was red without an assertion failure. Preserve all gates while giving coverage and static independent bounded jobs."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,nightly,quality-gates,timeout
created_at: "2026-09-23T19:19:12.555Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-23T20:52:42.689Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-23T20:50:55.925Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-23T20:50:55.925Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Ubuntu Node 24 coverage and static quality run in independent bounded jobs; Windows Node 24 runs the complete test suite across two independently bounded shards; all version, secret, typecheck, compatibility, tracker, alerting and other platform checks remain required; recurrence policy requires both Windows shards; a hosted nightly run passes every job under its declared timeout."
parent: pm-u9d0
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions ubuntu-latest Node 24 Nightly Validation
repro_steps: "Dispatch nightly.yml on branch 544c19398; inspect run 35905763390: Ubuntu Node 24 Test with coverage gate passes, Static quality gate is canceled at 20 minutes during mutation."
resolution: "Separated Ubuntu exact coverage and full static quality into independent jobs, registered the new quality job, split the complete Windows test suite into two shards, and required both shards in recurrence policy."
expected_result: "Every nightly coverage, quality, platform, security, compatibility, tracker and alerting gate completes within its 20-minute job budget without lowering thresholds."
actual_result: "Run 35917009573 passed all seven jobs at 0e1270bc5; longest Ubuntu coverage was 13m30s, quality 8m44s, Windows shards 10m15s and 11m58s. Registry and workflow tests passed 24/24."
